{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.nucleon_ordering_factorization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.nucleon_ordering_factorization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.not_nucleonOrderingFactorization_of_free_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.not_nucleonOrderingFactorization_of_free_data","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/nucleon_ordering_factorization.lean#L172-L182","doc":"**The decomposition is refutable at freely-chosen data**, which is why it\nis named rather than carried as a `sorry`.\n\nAt `tr_M = 1` with every channel quantity zero it reads `1 = 0`.  Recorded\nas a theorem so a later attempt to \"finish\" this file by adding a `sorry`\nover free data fails against a standing counterexample — and so the\n2026-08-08 → `b67ee924e84` round trip cannot be repeated silently. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.trace_ordering_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.trace_ordering_independent","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/nucleon_ordering_factorization.lean#L146-L170","doc":"**Ordering independence of the Markov trace** — the proposition's actual\nconclusion, *derived* from the decomposition rather than assumed.\n\nTwo nucleon orderings related by a permutation, whose symmetric and\nalternating channels are the scalar products `∏ₖ fS(d_k)` and `∏ₖ fA(d_k)`\nof sub-claim (i) and which agree on the standard channel `z·a_π + b_π`,\ngive the same Markov trace.\n\nThis is why the decomposition is worth naming: it is a hypothesis something\nis proved **from**.  The standard channel is a `2 × 2` matrix product and is\n*not* ordering-independent in general, which is exactly why its agreement\nappears here as a hypothesis rather than as a lemma. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.nucleon_ordering_factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.nucleon_ordering_factorization","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/nucleon_ordering_factorization.lean#L133-L144","doc":"**The claim of `prop:nucleon-ordering-factorization`**, as a proposition\nover caller-supplied data:\n\n  `tr_M(𝒩) = W_sym · S(π) + W_std · (z · a_π + b_π) + W_alt · A(π)`.\n\n**Named, not asserted.**  See the module docstring for why neither a\nprojection nor a `sorry` is the honest form, and for what the master\nfactorisation would need in order to be derived. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:nucleon-ordering-factorization","label":"prop:nucleon-ordering-factorization","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/nucleon-ordering-factorization.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.scalar_channel_ordering_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.scalar_channel_ordering_independent","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/nucleon_ordering_factorization.lean#L113-L131","doc":"**Scalar-channel ordering independence (derived).**\n\nSub-claim (i) of the proposition: the symmetric / alternating channel\nvalue `∏ₖ f(d_k)` is a product of commuting scalars, so it is invariant\nunder any reordering `π → π'` of the nucleon sequence.  Here `ds`/`ds'`\nare the per-nucleon channel data and `f` is the scalar map\n(`f d = q + d` for `S`, `f d = −q⁻¹ + d` for `A`).\n\nProved by `List.Perm.prod_eq` — real content, not a projection.\n\n§7c: stated over a generic commutative monoid.  Permutation-invariance of a\nproduct uses no ordering, no radical and no `Real.*` construct, so `ℝ` bought\nnothing here; the channel data and the scalar map may even live in different\ntypes.  The archimedean instance is recovered at `α := ℝ`, `M := ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}